.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: ISC
.Dd June 14, 2026
.Dt MBT_PACK 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_pack ,
.Nm mbt_unpack
.Nd Wire format pack/unpack helpers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/pack.h
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_pack "unsigned char *out" "char *v" "..."
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_unpack "unsigned char *in" "char *v" "..."
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Provides helpers for encoding and decoding data in a specific wire format.
These functions use a format string to specify how data should be packed into or
unpacked from buffers.
.Pp
The following format characters are supported:
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It 'b'
1 byte.
    .Bl -tag -width 1
    .It pack
Pass an `int` argument.
    .It unpack
Populate an `unsigned char *out` pointer.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It 'l'
4 bytes, big-endian.
    .Bl -tag -width 1
    .It pack
Pass a `uint32_t` argument.
    .It unpack
Populate a `uint32_t *out` pointer.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It '*'
Raw bytes.
    .Bl -tag -width 1
    .It pack
Pass `size_t len` and `void *data`.
    .It unpack
Expected `int len` is provided, populates an `unsigned char *out` pointer.
.El
.Pp
.Fn mbt_pack
encodes data into the buffer pointed to by
.Fa out
using the format string
.Fa v.
Returns the number of bytes produced.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_unpack
decodes data from the buffer pointed to
to by
.Fa in
using the format string
.Fa v.
Returns the number of bytes consumed.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Both functions return the number of bytes processed (produced for `mbt_pack`,
consumed for `mbt_unpack`). A negative value indicates an error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Packing and unpacking a byte and a 32-bit integer:
.Bd -literal
unsigned char buf[64];
unsigned char out_buf[64];
int n;

// Pack a byte (0x42) and a uint32 (0x12345678)
n = mbt_pack(buf, "bl", 0x42, 0x12345678);

// Unpack it
unsigned char b;
uint32_t l;
if (mbt_unpack(buf, "bl", &b, &l) > 0) {
    // b is 0x42, l is 0x12345678
}
.Ed
